description:
Here's a minified test case from `hereby`:
ts
// @verbatimModuleSyntax: true
// @module: node16
// @moduleResolution: node16
// @target: es2018
// @filename: package.json
{ "name": "foo", "type": "module" }
// @filename: index.ts
class Task {}
function task(): Task { return new Task(); }
export const build = task();
export default build;
With this, I get:
 export default build;
 ~~~~~
!!! error TS1284: An 'export default' must reference a value when 'verbatimModuleSyntax' is enabled, but 'build' only refers to a type.
But, `build` isn't a type, it's a value.

text:
Bug Title: An 'export default' must reference a value when 'verbatimModuleSyntax' is enabled, but export is a value
Bug Description: Here's a minified test case from `hereby`:
ts
// @verbatimModuleSyntax: true
// @module: node16
// @moduleResolution: node16
// @target: es2018
// @filename: package.json
{ "name": "foo", "type": "module" }
// @filename: index.ts
class Task {}
function task(): Task { return new Task(); }
export const build = task();
export default build;
With this, I get:
 export default build;
 ~~~~~
!!! error TS1284: An 'export default' must reference a value when 'verbatimModuleSyntax' is enabled, but 'build' only refers to a type.
But, `build` isn't a type, it's a value.

