# Bug Report
<!--
 Please fill in each section completely. Thank you!
-->
 🔎 Search Terms
Enum, declaration, d.ts, renaming of 'enum'
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- This is a crash (sort of, .d.ts is "corrupt")
- This changed between versions v4.7.4 and v4.8.4
 ⏯ Playground Link
[Playground link with relevant code](
 💻 Code
ts
type Props = {
 enum: boolean;
 one: boolean;
};
function omitEnum({ enum: myEnum, ...rest }: Props) {
 return rest
}
 🙁 Actual behavior
`.d.ts` in `v4.8.4` and later
ts
declare type Props = {
 enum: boolean;
 one: boolean;
 two: boolean;
};
declare function omitEnum({ enum, ...rest }: Props): {
 one: boolean;
 two: boolean;
};
Because `enum` isn't re-assigned, TypeScript complains with `':' expected.`
 🙂 Expected behavior
`.d.ts` in `v4.7.4`
ts
declare type Props = {
 enum: boolean;
 one: boolean;
 two: boolean;
};
declare function omitEnum({ enum: myEnum, ...rest }: Props): {
 one: boolean;
 two: boolean;
};

