# Bug Report
I've read #10676, but I'm failing to understand why there is no consistent widening accross the 3 examples mentioned below. 🔎 Search Terms
* literal * widening
* union
* generics
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
AFAIK not a regression. ⏯ Playground Link
[Playground link with relevant code](
 💻 Code
<!-- Please post the relevant code sample here as well-->
ts
class FormControl<T> {
 constructor(t:T extends undefined ? never : T) {}
}
const a = new FormControl('');
// ^? FormControl<string>
class FormControl2<T> {
 constructor(t:T|string) {}
}
const b = new FormControl2("");
// ^? FormControl<string>
class FormControl3<T> {
 constructor(t:T extends undefined ? never : (T|string)) {}
}
const c = new FormControl3("");
// ^? FormControl<"">
 🙁 Actual behavior
Non consistant behaviour between use-cases. 🙂 Expected behavior
Consistent behaviour.

