Bug Title: Organize Imports doesn't treat exports the same way and merges groups
Bug Description: <!-- ⚠️⚠️ Do Not Delete This! bug_report_template ⚠️⚠️ -->
<!-- Please read our Rules of Conduct: -->
<!-- 🕮 Read our guide about submitting issues: -->
<!-- 🔎 Search existing issues to avoid creating duplicates. -->
<!-- 🧪 Test using the latest Insiders build to see if your issue has already been fixed: -->
<!-- 💡 Instead of creating your report here, use 'Report Issue' from the 'Help' menu in VS Code to pre-fill useful information. -->
<!-- 🔧 Launch with `code --disable-extensions` to check. -->
Does this issue occur when all extensions are disabled?: Yes
<!-- 🪓 If you answered No above, use 'Help: Start Extension Bisect' from Command Palette to try to identify the cause. -->
<!-- 📣 Issues caused by an extension need to be reported directly to the extension publisher. The 'Help > Report Issue' dialog can assist with this. -->
- VS Code Version: 1.75.1
- OS Version: macOS 13.2.1
Steps to Reproduce:
1. Write a TypeScript file like the following:
 typescript
 export { C } from "./C";
 export { B } from "./B";
 export { A } from "./A";
 export { bFuncC } from "./C";
 export { bFuncB } from "./B";
 export { bFuncA } from "./A";
 3. Execute the Organize Imports command.
I expect the file to look like this:
typescript
export { A } from "./A";
export { B } from ".B";
export { C } from "./C";
export { bFuncA } from "./A";
export { bFuncB } from "./B";
export { bFuncC } from "./C";
Instead, it looks like this:
typescript
export { A, bFuncA } from "./A";
export { B, bFuncB } from ".B";
export { bFuncC, C } from "./C";

