description:
# Bug Report
We wanted to migrate to the new native decorators when upgrading to typescript 5, but ran into problem.
I get a runtime error when I pass a static variable of the same class to the class decorator. It seems that static members are initializing **after** decorator execution.
 🔎 Search Terms
- decorators
- decorators static
- es decorators
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
Typescript 5+and es decorators. ExperimentalDecorators works well with similar code.
 ⏯ Playground Link
<!--
 A link to a TypeScript Playground "Share" link which shows this behavior
 The TypeScript Workbench can be used for more complex setups, try
 As a last resort, you can link to a repo, but these will be slower for us to investigate.
-->
[Playground link with relevant code](
 💻 Code
<!-- Please post the relevant code sample here as well-->
ts
function defineCustomElement(name: string) {
 return (target: CustomElementConstructor, context: ClassDecoratorContext) => {
 customElements.define(name, target);
 };
}
@defineCustomElement(CustomElement.TAGNAME)
class CustomElement extends HTMLElement{
 public static TAGNAME = "custom-tag";
}
const instance = new CustomElement();
 🙁 Actual behavior
Runtime Error: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'TAGNAME') 🙂 Expected behavior
Run without errors.

