description:
# Bug Report
In auditing some code, I've noticed something that doesn't seem like it should compile. In >=4.95, the following code compiles without an issue, but in <=4.7.4, there is an error. Why is it possible to specify an object for the name of a parameter? This code was likely the result of a bad copy/paste, but TS isn't erroring on it. Am I missing something about the syntax? Also, is the discrepancy between versions intended? ts repro
const DEFAULT_NUM_PAGINATED_RESULTS = 10;
type IPaginatedParams = {first?: number; after?: string;}
type GetPaginatedResults = <Obj, Key extends keyof Obj>(
 items: Obj[],
 { first = DEFAULT_NUM_PAGINATED_RESULTS, after }: IPaginatedParams,
 key: Key
 ) => { items: Obj[]; hasMore: boolean };
Playground links for [4.7.4]( vs [4.9.5](
 🔎 Search Terms
function parameter names

