description:
# Bug Report
 🔎 Search Terms
systemjs if var
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- This is the behavior in every version I tried
 ⏯ Playground Link
[Playground link with relevant code](
 💻 Code
ts
if (false) {
 var y = 1;
}
function f() {
 console.log(y);
}
export { y };
 🙁 Actual behavior
js
System.register([], function (exports_1, context_1) {
 "use strict";
 var __moduleName = context_1 && context_1.id;
 function f() {
 console.log(y);
 }
 return {
 setters: [],
 execute: function () {
 if (false) {
 var y = 1;
 }
 }
 };
});
- `f` is hoisted out of the `execute` function containing the module body.
- `y` is not hoisted.
- `y` is not exported.
 🙂 Expected behavior
js
System.register([], function (exports_1, context_1) {
 "use strict";
 var y;
 var __moduleName = context_1 && context_1.id;
 function f() {
 console.log(y);
 }
 return {
 setters: [],
 execute: function () {
 if (false) {
 y = 1;
 exports_1("y", y);
 }
 }
 };
});
- `f` is hoisted out of the `execute` function containing the module body.
- `y` is hoisted out of the `execute` function containing the module body.
- `y` is exported.
It looks like we are not traversing into top-level `if` statements, though we do properly descend into top-level `for`, `for-in`, `for-of`, `do`, `while`, `with`, `switch`, `try`, blocks, and labeled statements.

