description:
# Bug Report
The child class should not be able to access the class field defined by the parent class via super
 🔎 Search Terms
class field super parent
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
Happens on 5.1.0-beta
 ⏯ Playground Link
[Playground link with relevant code](
 💻 Code
<!-- Please post the relevant code sample here as well-->
ts
class T {
 field = () => {}
}
class T2 extends T {
 f() {
 super.field()
// ~~~~~~~~~~~
 }
}
new T2().f()
 🙁 Actual behavior
No type error
 🙂 Expected behavior
Type error.
`super` will look for the parent class, but the class field is always defined on the current instance.

js
export class C {
 updateDisplay() {
 }
}
export class D extends C {
 updateDisplay() {
 }
}
The generated d.ts for JS has `export class D extends C {}` whereas TS has `export declare class D extends C { updateDisplay(): void }`

