After correctly narrowing the type of `this` using type coercion (I think that's the proper term) it works correctly in the local scope, but an arrow function which is declared in the same scope won't know what `this` is. Replacing the `this: CorrectObject | WrongObject` argument in `problemFunction` with `myValue: CorrectObject | WrongObject` works as expected, it's only broken when using `this`.
