description:
Here's `hello.ts`:
ts
import { World } from "./world";
export function getHello() {
 return "hello";
}
export function getWorld(): World {
 return "world";
}
Here's `world.ts`
ts
export type World = "world";
Notice there is a trailing newline in `world.ts`.
Move `getWorld` to `world.ts`, and what you will get is
ts
import { World } from "./world";
export type World = "world";export function getWorld(): World {
 return "world";
}
Notice that `getWorld` is not given its own line, and there are two trailing newlines.
What would be expected is:
ts
import { World } from "./world";
export type World = "world";
export function getWorld(): World {
 return "world";
}

