description:
# Bug Report
 🔎 Search Terms
`TypedPropertyDescriptor`
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
4.9.5, likely before.
 ⏯ Playground Link
[Playground link with relevant code](
 💻 Code
typescript
function propertyDescriptorToTypedPropertyDescriptor<T>(foo: PropertyDescriptor): TypedPropertyDescriptor<T> {
 return foo;
}
produces error.
This is due to the small difference between interfaces: typescript
interface PropertyDescriptor {
 ...
 get?(): any;
 set?(v: any): void;
}
typescript
interface TypedPropertyDescriptor<T> {
 get?: () => T;
 set?: (value: T) => void;
}
in `PropertyDescriptor`, the `get?(): any` allows `undefined` as a value. In `TypedPropertyDescriptor`, `get?: () => T` only allows skipping the value but not passing `undefined`.
Likely the former is correct (but I haven't looked at the spec so not 100% sure).
 🙁 Actual behavior
Code produces error with `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` set to `true`.
 🙂 Expected behavior
Code compiles with `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` set to `true`.

