description:
# Bug Report
Adding a common "typeRoots" key on an extended configuration is not taking into account anymore. We discussed it a little bit on this PR: 🕗 Version & Regression Information
it used to work on the v `5.0.4` but it stopped working when I migrted to `5.1.3`.
 🙁 Actual behavior
I have a global tsconfig json file as following: json
// base.json
{
 "$schema": "
 "compilerOptions": {
 "typeRoots": ["../../node_modules/@types"]
 }
}
And I'm using it within my monorepo on each package as following: json
{
 "extends": "@slowy/config/tsconfig/base.json",
 "compilerOptions": {
 "typeRoots": [ "../../node_modules/@types"]
 },
}
However as you can see, I have to re-declare the typeRoots option which was not necessary before the library update. 🙂 Expected behavior
Being able to extend the typeRoots configuration. Thanks!

