description:
# Suggestion
Add `invalidate(fileName: string, kind: FileWatcherEventKind)` to WatchProgram.
ts
export interface Watch<T> {
 /** Synchronize with host and get updated program */
 getProgram(): T;
 /** Manual invalidation for custom sys */
 + invalidate(fileName: string, kind: FileWatcherEventKind): void;
}
The invalidation mechanism is hidden inside the WatchProgram and cannot be controlled from the outside.
I already implement this [here]( but I I haven't made a pull request yet.
## 🔍 Search Terms
createWatchProgarm, WatchProgram, invalidate, cache, ResolutionCache
## ✅ Viability Checklist
My suggestion meets these guidelines:
* [x] This wouldn't be a breaking change in existing TypeScript/JavaScript code
* [x] This wouldn't change the runtime behavior of existing JavaScript code
* [x] This could be implemented without emitting different JS based on the types of the expressions
* [x] This isn't a runtime feature (e.g. library functionality, non-ECMAScript syntax with JavaScript output, new syntax sugar for JS, etc.)
* [x] This feature would agree with the rest of [TypeScript's Design Goals](
## ⭐ Suggestion
Add manual invalidation feature to WatchProgram.
## 📃 Motivating Example
I was trying to create an optimizer based on TypeScript that performs multi-step transformations using an in-memory cache. The normal watch program is useful for development on an editor, but an environment based on reading and writing filesystems is overkill for multi-step source transformations.
We wanted to use a bundler-like environment like Rollup to update the source for transformations on top of virtual memory.
In order to reproduce the normal TypeScript project environment as much as possible, we tried to create a system that reads from memory only the first time and falls back to an in-memory cache thereafter, and pass this to WatchProgram.
However, this made external Invalidation impossible because the ResolutionCache was hidden inside.
This callback is fired on file state change. `in src/compiler/watch.ts`
ts
 function onSourceFileChange(fileName: string, eventKind: FileWatcherEventKind, path: Path) {
 updateCachedSystemWithFile(fileName, path, eventKind);
 // Update the source file cache
 if (eventKind FileWatcherEventKind.Deleted && sourceFilesCache.has(path)) {
 resolutionCache.invalidateResolutionOfFile(path);
 }
 nextSourceFileVersion(path);
 // Update the program
 scheduleProgramUpdate();
 }
`resolutionCache` is local scope variable in `createWatchProgram` so I can not touch directly.
ts
 // Cache for the module resolution
 const resolutionCache = createResolutionCache(compilerHost,
 configFileName ?
 getDirectoryPath(getNormalizedAbsolutePath(configFileName, currentDirectory)) :
 currentDirectory,
 /*logChangesWhenResolvingModule*/ false
 );
`ResolutionCache.invalidateResolutionOfFile()` is also internal method in typescript.
## 💻 Use Cases
My trying code is here.
ts
import ts from "typescript";
import path from "node:path";
const tsconfig = ts.readConfigFile("./tsconfig.json", ts.sys.readFile);
const options = ts.parseJsonConfigFileContent(tsconfig.config, ts.sys, "./");
let _watchCallback: ts.FileWatcherCallback | null = null;
type FileInfo = {
 path: string;
 content: string;
 version: number;
 sourceFile?: ts.SourceFile;
 mtime?: Date;
};
const _cache = new Map<string, FileInfo>();
const _dirtyCacheSet = new Set<string>();
const expandPath = (fname: string) => {
 if (fname.startsWith("/")) {
 return fname;
 }
 const root = host.getCurrentDirectory();
 return path.join(root, fname);
};
function readFile(fname: string, encode?: any) {
 fname = expandPath(fname);
 console.log("[readFile]", fname);
 // console.log("[host:readFile]", fname);
 if (_cache.has(fname)) {
 return _cache.get(fname)?.content as string;
 }
 const ret = ts.sys.readFile(fname, encode);
 if (ret) {
 _cache.set(fname, {
 path: fname,
 content: ret,
 version: 0,
 mtime: ts.sys.getModifiedTime?.(fname),
 });
 _dirtyCache.add(fname);
 }
 return ret;
}
const writeFile = (fname: string, content: string) => {
 fname = expandPath(fname);
 console.log("[writeFile]", fname);
 const fileInfo = _cache.get(fname);
 if (fileInfo) {
 fileInfo.content = content;
 fileInfo.version++;
 fileInfo.mtime = new Date();
 }
 _dirtyCache.add(fname);
 _watchCallback?.(fname, ts.FileWatcherEventKind.Changed);
};
const watchFile = (
 path: string,
 callback: ts.FileWatcherCallback,
 options: any,
) => {
 if (_watchCallback == null) {
 _watchCallback = callback;
 }
 return {
 close() {},
 };
};
const watchDirectory = (path: string, callback: ts.FileWatcherCallback) => {
 if (_watchCallback == null) {
 _watchCallback = callback;
 }
 return { close() {} };
};
const mySys: ts.System = {
 ...ts.sys,
 readFile,
 writeFile,
 watchFile,
 watchDirectory,
};
const host = ts.createWatchCompilerHost(
 options.fileNames,
 options.options,
 mySys,
 ts.createSemanticDiagnosticsBuilderProgram,
);
const watcher = ts.createWatchProgram(host);
// pre check
console.log(watcher.getProgram().getSemanticDiagnostics()[0].messageText);
// update in memory file
writeFile(
 path.join(process.cwd(), "src/index.ts"),
 "export const a = 1;",
);
// If this pr merged, we can use this to invalidate internal cache
// watcher.invalidate(path.join(process.cwd(), "src/index.ts"), ts.FileWatcherEventKind.Changed);
// can not update source without internal invalidation
const newSource = watcher.getProgram().getSourceFile(
 path.join(process.cwd(), "src/index.ts"),
);
// old source yet
console.log("newSource", newSource?.getFullText());
// post check: should be no error
console.log(watcher.getProgram().getSemanticDiagnostics()[0].messageText);

