description:
Type: <b>Bug</b>
Take the two files:
 `1.ts`
ts
export class Bar {}
export class Baz {}
 `2.ts`
ts
import { Bar, Baz } from "./1.ts";
const Foo = {
 bar: Bar,
 baz: Baz,
}
export function GetFoo(name:keyof typeof Foo) {
 return Foo[name];
}
If you then try and select the `Foo` and refactor > move to file > `1.ts`, will cause `1.ts` to become:
ts
import { Bar, Baz } from "./1.ts"; // <- bad!
export class Bar {}
export class Baz {}
export const Foo = {
 bar: Bar,
 baz: Baz,
};
As you can see `1.ts` is trying to import itsself, which results in the error message (which in TypeScript fashion, is borderline incomprehensible): Individual declarations in merged declaration 'Bar' must be all exported or all local.
VS Code version: Code - Insiders 1.84.0-insider (Universal) (6a7a661757dec1983ff05ef908a2bbb75ce841e0, )
OS version: Darwin x64 21.6.0
Modes:
<!-- generated by issue reporter -->

text:
Bug Title: TypeScript "Move to File" refactor causes self import
Bug Description: Type: <b>Bug</b>
Take the two files:
 `1.ts`
ts
export class Bar {}
export class Baz {}
 `2.ts`
ts
import { Bar, Baz } from "./1.ts";
const Foo = {
 bar: Bar,
 baz: Baz,
}
export function GetFoo(name:keyof typeof Foo) {
 return Foo[name];
}
If you then try and select the `Foo` and refactor > move to file > `1.ts`, will cause `1.ts` to become:
ts
import { Bar, Baz } from "./1.ts"; // <- bad!
export class Bar {}
export class Baz {}
export const Foo = {
 bar: Bar,
 baz: Baz,
};
As you can see `1.ts` is trying to import itsself, which results in the error message (which in TypeScript fashion, is borderline incomprehensible): Individual declarations in merged declaration 'Bar' must be all exported or all local.
VS Code version: Code - Insiders 1.84.0-insider (Universal) (6a7a661757dec1983ff05ef908a2bbb75ce841e0, )
