 Bar[Bar["B"] = 10] = "B";
 Bar[Bar["C"] = 11] = "C";
})(Bar || (Bar = {}));
 🙂 Expected behavior
Emit a warning or an error, and generate code that does not rely on other imports.
Example:
JavaScript
import { Foo } from "./foo";
export var Bar;
(function(Bar) {
 Bar[Bar["B"] = Foo.A] = "B";
 Bar[Bar["C"] = void 0] = "C";
})(Bar || (Bar = {}));
The Bar.C is void 0, since it cannot be refered.
 Additional information about the issue
