description:
🔎 Search Terms
auto fix namespace enum 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- This feature "add missing properties" is new in v4.4 which also has the bug.
 ⏯ Playground Link
 💻 Code
ts
namespace Hmi.Events {
 export enum Type {
 Message = 0,
 Alarm = 1,
 }
 export interface Message {
 prop1: string;
 prop2: number;
 prop3: Type.Message;
 prop4: Hmi.Events.Type.Message;
 }
}
let message0: Hmi.Events.Message = {
 // ^- apply "add missing properties" on that
}
// results in following code with invalid "Type":
let message1: Hmi.Events.Message = {
 prop1: "",
 prop2: 0,
 prop3: Type.Message,
 prop4: Type.Message
}
// should be this:
let message2: Hmi.Events.Message = {
 prop1: "",
 prop2: 0,
 prop3: Hmi.Events.Type.Message,
 prop4: Hmi.Events.Type.Message
}
 🙁 Actual behavior
The created properties was copied verbatim from the Typescript AST which is in its normalized form without namespace.
But this is not valid at the target place `Type.Message`.
 🙂 Expected behavior
The enum value should be corrected with the full namespace `Hmi.Events.Type.Message`.
 Additional information about the issue
_No response_

