description:
js
/** @type {unique symbol} */
const s = Symbol()
/** @typedef {{ [s]: boolean }} A - should be OK in JS */
/** @type {unique symbol} */
const v = Symbol()
/** @typedef {{ [key: v]: boolean }} D - should error in JS */
compare to TS
ts
const t: unique symbol = Symbol()
type B = { [t]: boolean } // should be OK in TS (and is)
const u: unique symbol = Symbol()
type C = { [key: u]: boolean } // should error in TS (and does)
It appears as if `s` and `v` have type `symbol` not `unique symbol`.

