description:
🔎 Search Terms
"organize imports assert", "organize imports with", "organize imports assertions", "organize imports attributes"
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- This is the behavior in every version I tried, and I reviewed the FAQ for entries about "organize imports"
 ⏯ Playground Link
Playground doesn't support organize imports as far as I can tell.
 💻 Code
In VSCode run the organize imports command on the following code:
ts
import { A } from "./file";
import { type B } from "./file";
import { C } from "./file" assert { type: "a" };
import { A as D } from "./file" assert { type: "b" };
import { E } from "./file" with { type: "a" };
import { A as F } from "./file" with { type: "b" };
type G = A | B | C | D | E | F;
 🙁 Actual behavior
Currently, organize imports will combine all the imports to the following line:
ts
import { A, C, A as D, E, A as F, type B } from "./file";
type G = A | B | C | D | E | F;
 🙂 Expected behavior
As import attributes can change the behavior of the imported module they should stay as separate lines:
ts
import { A, type B } from "./file";
import { C } from "./file" assert { type: "a" };
import { A as D } from "./file" assert { type: "b" };
import { E } from "./file" with { type: "a" };
import { A as F } from "./file" with { type: "b" };
type G = A | B | C | D | E | F;
 Additional information about the issue
_No response_

