description:
🔎 Search Terms
eval, strict mode, namespace
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- This is the behavior in every version I tried
 ⏯ Playground Link
 💻 Code
ts
declare global {
 export namespace myNamespace {
 export function eval(): void;
 }
}
export {}
 🙁 Actual behavior
Invalid use of 'eval'. Modules are automatically in strict mode.
 🙂 Expected behavior
No error
 Additional information about the issue
I see in that this behavior is by design as defining an 'eval' function is forbidden in strict mode. However, the namespace declaration above describes runtime code more like the following, which is perfectly valid in strict mode:
ts
const myNamespace = {
 eval() {
 // ...
 }
}
Would it be possible to not fail on namespaced function declarations?

