- This is the behavior in every version I tried
 ⏯ Playground Link
 💻 Code
ts
new class A extends class { a() {} } {
 constructor() {
 super();
 let after;
 class B {
 @(after = super.a, (_1, _2) => {}) f = "";
 }
 after();
 }
}
 🙁 Actual behavior
TS complains that:
- I'm accessing `super.a` before calling `super()`
- I'm calling `after` before initializing it
 🙂 Expected behavior
That code should be fine
