description:
🔎 Search Terms
`using`
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
I assume this bug has existed since `using` was implemented.
 ⏯ Playground Link
 💻 Code
ts
let blockValues: any[] = [];
function TestUsingInBlock() {
 {
 using x = {
 value: 1,
 [Symbol.dispose]() {
 blockValues.push(42);
 }
 };
 console.log(x);
 blockValues.push(43);
 }
}
TestUsingInBlock();
console.log(blockValues);
 🙁 Actual behavior
The type system does not correctly infer the type of the object literal on the RHS of a `using` and reports the error "Object literal may only specify known properties, and 'value' does not exist in type 'Disposable'."
 🙂 Expected behavior
I expect `using` declarations to work with object literals.
 Additional information about the issue
cc @rbuckton

