description:
🔎 Search Terms
infer function argument bug
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- I think this is a bug
- I could not find a change between versions
 ⏯ Playground Link
 💻 Code
ts
interface Action<Value> {
 _run(input: Value): Value;
}
function minLength<Value extends string | any[]>(
 min: number
): Action<Value> {
 return {
 _run(input) {
 if (input.length < min) {
 throw new Error('minLength');
 }
 return input;
 },
 };
}
// Version 1 (the one with an error)
function pipe1<
 TAction1 extends Action<string>,
>(action1: TAction1): (input: string) => string {
 return (input) => action1._run(input);
}
const Schema1 = pipe1(minLength(1)); // TS should infer `string` from the outer function
// Version 2 (it works when wrapped in a tuple)
function pipe2<
 TAction1 extends [Action<string>],
>(action1: TAction1): (input: string) => string {
 return (input) => action1[0]._run(input);
}
const Schema2 = pipe2([minLength(1)]); // Here it works as expected
 🙁 Actual behavior
In certain cases, TS will not infer the type of the inner function based on the outer function automatically and will display an error instead. In other cases, such as when the type is wrapped in a tuple, it works. That's why I think the current behavior is inconsistent. Maybe there's a reason for this that I'm not aware of, otherwise it could be a bug.
 🙂 Expected behavior
I would expect TS to infer the type and not show an error. TS should have all the information it needs to infer the type automatically.
 Additional information about the issue
I discovered this problem while rewriting the source code of Valibot:

