description:
🔎 Search Terms
filename, noImplicitAny, TS7018, 7018
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- This is the behavior in every version I tried, and I reviewed the FAQ for entries about TS7018, line number, filename
 ⏯ Playground Link
 💻 Code
ts
function doSthWithParams(params: unknown) {
 if (typeof params !== 'object') {
 return {};
 }
 return {
 c: 'foo',
 p: 'bar',
 s: 'baz',
 };
}
const bar = {
 p: null,
 s: null,
 ...doSthWithParams({
 p: 'hello',
 s: 'world',
 }),
};
 🙁 Actual behavior
We're trying to incrementally get our codebase toward the strict mode. When we've enabled `noImplicitAny` flag we got an error that was very hard to track as it didn't give a file and line number where the error happens. Object literal's property 'p' implicitly has an 'any' type.
Object literal's property 's' implicitly has an 'any' type.
 🙂 Expected behavior
The TS compiler error should point to a file and line number where the error occurs
 Additional information about the issue
This happens if `noImplicitAny` is true and `strictNullChecks` is not yet enabled

