description:
🔎 Search Terms
jsdoc tag inherit
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- This is the behavior in every version I tried
 ⏯ Playground Link
 💻 Code
ts
class A {
 /** * Description text here.
 * * @virtual
 * */
 foo() { }
}
class B extends A {
 override foo() { }
}
class C extends B {
 override foo() { }
}
 🙁 Actual behavior
Only the description text is provided for `C.foo`.
 🙂 Expected behavior
Both the description text and the tag should be provided for `C.foo`, just as the behavior of `B.foo`.
 Additional information about the issue
I'm trying to provide a solution for by using typescript-eslint + JSDoc tag. This bug makes `@virtual` tag disappear and I will not be able to override `C.foo` in "strict-virtual" mode.
Also note that `@inheritdoc` tag doesn't work here. Adding `@inheritdoc` to `B.foo` will only provide `@inheritdoc` itself to `C.foo`, instead of the `@virtual` tag, which is an unexpected and unuseful behavior.

