description:
🔎 Search Terms
transpile declaration api emit enum missing
 🕗 Version & Regression Information
- This changed in commit or PR @weswigham ⏯ Playground Link
 💻 Code
ts repro
// @strict: true
// @declaration: true
// @showEmit
// @showEmittedFile: a.d.ts
// @showEmittedFile: b.d.ts
// @filename: a.ts
export enum Foo {
 A = 'a',
 B = 'b',
}
// @filename: b.ts
import {Foo} from './a';
export type Bar = {
 [Foo.A]: 1;
 [Foo.B]: 2;
}
[Workbench Repro](
 🙁 Actual behavior
Refer to this program which invokes the `ts.transpileDeclaration` API:
Basic instructions to invoke it can be found in
When using the API, `b.d.ts` is emitted as
ts
export type Bar = {};
while when using `tsc` it gets emitted as
ts
import { Foo } from './a';
export type Bar = {
 [Foo.A]: 1;
 [Foo.B]: 2;
};
 🙂 Expected behavior
Using the API should emit
ts
import { Foo } from './a';
export type Bar = {
 [Foo.A]: 1;
 [Foo.B]: 2;
};
 Additional information about the issue
It's entirely possible that usage of the API is incorrect, though it doesn't seem to deviate from the patterns demonstrated in

